{"type":"assistant.message","data":{"messageId":"b89795b9-6885-40fb-9643-032db01a38d6","content":"Here's the build failure analysis:\n\n## Solution Structure\n```\nBuildDiag.sln\n├── Core (net8.0)        — no dependencies\n├── Services (net8.0)    — references Core\n└── Api (net8.0, exe)    — references Services + Core\n```\n\n## Root Cause Error (1 issue, 2 symptoms)\n\n**`Services/UserService.cs` — missing NuGet package `Newtonsoft.Json`**\n\nThe `Services` project uses `Newtonsoft.Json` types but has **no `PackageReference`** for it in `Services.csproj`. This produces two CS0246 errors:\n\n| Error | File | Message |\n|-------|------|---------|\n| CS0246 | `Services/UserService.cs` | The type or namespace name **'Newtonsoft'** could not be found |\n| CS0246 | `Services/UserService.cs` | The type or namespace name **'JObject'** could not be found |\n\n## Cascading Failure\n\n**`Api` project never compiled.** It depends on `Services` via `<ProjectReference>`, so when `Services` failed to compile, MSBuild skipped building `Api` entirely. This is **not a separate bug** — it will resolve once Services builds.\n\n## Fix\n\nAdd the missing NuGet package to `Services/Services.csproj`:\n\n```xml\n<ItemGroup>\n  <ProjectReference Include=\"..\\Core\\Core.csproj\" />\n</ItemGroup>\n+<ItemGroup>\n+  <PackageReference Include=\"Newtonsoft.Json\" Version=\"13.0.3\" />\n+</ItemGroup>\n```\n\nThen rebuild. The `Core` project compiled successfully, so no changes are needed there.","toolRequests":[],"interactionId":"3667bf23-1b83-4619-a739-0cc844d3e10d","outputTokens":416,"requestId":"0400:1D8AAF:7F1F7B1:8CA0F39:6A504577"},"id":"7587d5f5-be34-40e7-a1b2-67d0b39d3df5","timestamp":"2026-07-10T01:06:08.806Z","parentId":"0dfad37e-2582-4457-96ec-438b9d16b7e6"}
